.TH WISP 1 "2026-08-17" "wisp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wisp \- a lightweight text editor written in rust and lua
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wisp
.RI [ file " | " directory " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wisp
is a pure\-rust rewrite of rxi's lite: a small, fast editor whose entire
interface \(em views, syntax, commands, plugins \(em is lua, editable
while the editor runs.
.PP
Each
.I directory
argument becomes the project the editor opens; the last one wins. Each
.I file
argument is opened in a view. A path that does not exist yet is opened
as an empty buffer, and the first save creates it; if the directory that
would hold it is missing, the path is reported in the log instead.
.PP
With no arguments wisp opens the directory it was launched from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary on standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version on standard output and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat every remaining argument as a path, even one beginning with a dash.
.PP
An unrecognized option is reported on standard error and wisp exits with
status 2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wisp/init.lua
The user module, run after the plugins load. Created on first start.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wisp/plugins/
User plugins. Searched before the bundled ones, so a file here of the
same name replaces the shipped plugin.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/wisp/
The unpacked editor. Rewritten whenever the version changes; nothing of
the user's is kept here.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/wisp/
What the editor writes for itself:
.IR error.txt ,
and temporary files, which are swept at start.
.TP
.I .wisp_project.lua
Read from the project directory if present. Never written.
.PP
The directories default to
.IR ~/.config ,
.I ~/.local/share
and
.I ~/.local/state
as usual. A relative value is invalid per the base directory
specification and is ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WISP_SCALE
Overrides the display scale wisp would otherwise detect \(em what 100%
means. Runtime zoom
.RB ( ctrl +
.BR = ", " ctrl + \- ", " ctrl + 0 )
is relative to it.
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell the built\-in terminal runs.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT ", " SIGHUP
Shut down cleanly. Any unsaved document is written beside its original
with a
.B ~
suffix before the editor exits.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 2
An unrecognized command line option.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full documentation lives with the source, notably
.I DEVIATIONS.md
\(em every deliberate difference from lite's lua layer.
.SH AUTHORS
wisp is written by dvh, after rxi's lite.
